      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For dark chocolate, you generally need to melt it to 32-34°C, then quickly cool it to a molding temperature around 27°C, where it must stay still for about 5 minutes to allow the stable crystal nuclei to form. Once fully set in the mold, the chocolate should be stored at a cool, stable 15-18°C without fluctuations after removal. This precise range ensures the cocoa butter locks into those irreversible, stable crystals, effectively preventing any blooming. Even minor deviations from this temperature window can lead to those white streaks I mentioned earlier.",
